# Drafted by Gemini (R11c play), edited.

~ hickock_pitch
george_hickock [smile]: Good folk, take a bench before the greasepaint dries! Tonight Hickock and Company present The Prince in Gold, a tragedy of crowns and treachery, right here on the inn stage.
quest the_play arrival
-> END

~ body
Narrator: Behind the painted canvas, Barnaby Quill slumps cold in his chair, a tin goblet rolled beside his boot and a bitter almond scent rising from his velvet collar.
alda_farnum [afraid]: Saints preserve us, he was supposed to go on at the bell, not lie there stiff in my back room!
quest the_play body
-> suspects

~ suspects
george_hickock [afraid]: Dead, our finest villain dead before the curtain rises! Some fiend has poisoned poor Barnaby, and the whole taproom is waiting for their tragedy!
* Question Lilian Vale -> lilian
* Question Olwen Pike -> olwen
* Examine the fallen cup -> cup
* Check Barnaby's pockets -> note
* [if flag.play_clue_cup and flag.play_clue_note] Say we have what we need -> accuse_menu

~ lilian
lilian_vale [angry]: Why are you staring at me as if I brewed the stuff? Yes, the scoundrel fleeced me of six silver crowns at cards an hour ago, and now I will never see a penny of it!
-> suspects

~ olwen
olwen_pike [neutral]: Mind where you tread, the hem of this royal cloak is fray enough without heavy boots on it. Barnaby liked his drink, and nobody kept count of what he poured.
* [Insight DC 14] Watch her hands -> olwen_tell | olwen_calm
* Leave her to her sewing -> suspects

~ olwen_tell
Narrator: At the mention of the cup, her thumb slips against the needle and she draws the thread tight with rapid, jerky stitches.
olwen_pike [weary]: A prop is just a prop until an actor makes a mess of it.
-> suspects

~ olwen_calm
Narrator: Her needle dips and rises through the gold braid in a steady, unbroken rhythm, never missing a stitch.
-> suspects

~ cup
Narrator: The battered tin goblet bears a dab of yellow paint on its base to mark it for the prop table, and its rim is still tacky with sweet, dark dregs.
set play_clue_cup
quest the_play suspects
-> suspects

~ note
Narrator: Tucked inside his waistcoat is a torn scrap of paper, demanding payment of an old debt to a woman named Mara before the company leaves the moor.
set play_clue_note
-> suspects

~ accuse_menu
george_hickock [weary]: Speak plainly, friends, if you know whose hand brought ruin to our stage.
* Accuse Olwen -> accuse_olwen
* Accuse Lilian -> accuse_lilian
* Not yet -> suspects

~ accuse_lilian
george_hickock [afraid]: Lilian, my star, tell me you did not trade our leading villain for a handful of card money!
lilian_vale [angry]: Oh, spare me your grand speeches, George, you cannot pin a murder on me without a shred of proof!
-> suspects

~ accuse_olwen
Narrator: Olwen sets her needle neatly into the pincushion and folds the heavy cloak across her lap.
olwen_pike [sad]: Mara was the sweetest voice we ever had, until Barnaby took her savings and left her to rot in a debtor's ditch. I set the banquet cup by his elbow, and he drank it greedy as ever.
set play_accused_olwen
quest the_play accused
-> finale_offer

~ finale_offer
george_hickock [weary]: A dark deed, yet the lanterns are lit and the benches are full! Take up Barnaby's cloak and read his lines, I beg you, or Hickock and Company is finished!
* Take Barnaby's part -> finale_play
* [Performance DC 13] Take Barnaby's part with flourish -> finale_great | finale_play
* Decline -> finale_cancel

~ finale_play
Narrator: You stumble over a verse or two with the script hidden in your sleeve, though the tavern crowd claps heartily enough when the cardboard crown hits the boards.
gold +25
set play_done
quest the_play solved
-> END

~ finale_great
Narrator: You snarl the villain's curses, and the taproom roars with boots and tankards as the curtain falls.
george_hickock [smile]: Bravo, my newfound players, a triumph worthy of the grandest halls!
gold +50
set play_done
quest the_play solved
-> END

~ finale_cancel
Narrator: The stage candles are pinched out, leaving tallow and cold dust while the actors pack in silence.
set play_done
quest the_play solved
-> END
